    <paragraph>In the following exercises, you are drawing from a deck containing only these 10 cards: $$\text{A} \heartsuit$$ , $$\text{A} \spadesuit$$ , $$\text{A} \clubsuit$$ , $$\text{A} \diamondsuit$$ , $$\text{K} \spadesuit$$ , $$\text{K} \clubsuit$$ , $$\text{Q} \heartsuit$$ , $$\text{Q} \spadesuit$$ , $$\text{J} \heartsuit$$ , $$\text{J} \spadesuit$$ .</paragraph>
    <exercise number="33" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Let $$E$$ be the event “draw an ace.” What is the probability of $$E$$ ? What are the odds in favor of $$E$$ ? What are the odds against $$E$$ ?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="34" has_solution="false">
